### Credit Card JSON Ruleset v2

#### 1. Root structure
- Root contains: `v`, `banks`
- `banks[]` contains bank objects (no bank appears more than once)
- Each bank may contain: `b`, `bn`, `p`, `m`, `g`

#### 2. Hierarchy
Inheritance order: **bank → group → card**
Lower levels inherit higher-level perks and milestones unless excluded (`x`) or overridden (`md`).

#### 3. Key meanings
| Key | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `b` | bankName |
| `n` | name |
| `nw` | cardNetwork |
| `t` | cardType |
| `af` | annualFee |
| `jf` | joiningFee |
| `fs` | feeWaiverSpend |
| `fm` | foreignMarkup |
| `rv` | rewardValue |
| `cl` | color |
| `cf` | confidence |
| `p` | perks |
| `m` | milestones |
| `g` | groups |
| `c` | cards |
| `x` | exclusions |
| `bn` | BIN/IIN metadata |
| `cv` | caveats |
| `vp` | visits/passes (for lounge) |
| `fl` | flag (free-text, used for special markers) |
| `cb` | co-brand merchant name (string) |

#### 4. Co-brand handling (NEW)
- Co-branded cards (Swiggy HDFC, Tata Neu HDFC, Amazon Pay ICICI, Flipkart Axis, IRCTC SBI, BPCL SBI, MakeMyTrip ICICI, Yatra SBI, etc.) are **NOT separate banks**.
- They are stored as **groups under the issuing bank**.
- Optional `cb` field at group/card level identifies the co-brand merchant.
- Example: `{"n":"Swiggy","cb":"Swiggy",...}` under HDFC Bank.

#### 5. Card type codes (`t`)
| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `en` | entry-level |
| `pr` | premium |
| `p` | platinum |
| `sp` | super-premium |
| `cb` | cashback |
| `lt` | lifetime-free |
| `co` | corporate |
| `se` | secured |
| `ft` | fintech (includes prepaid+credit-line hybrids and NBFC credit cards) |

#### 6. Network codes (`nw`)
| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `v` | Visa |
| `mc` | Mastercard |
| `rp` | RuPay |
| `amex` | American Express |
| `dc` | Diners Club |

#### 7. Reward types (`rt`)
| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `p` | points |
| `c` | cashback |
| `mi` | miles |
| `v` | voucher |
| `w` | waiver |
| `l` | lounge |
| `f` | fee waiver/EMI |
| `i` | insurance |
| `g` | golf |
| `co` | concierge |
| `s` | service (spa, salon, club memberships) ← NEW |
| `d` | discount (% off, not cashback) ← NEW |
| `b` | BOGO / buy-1-get-1 ← NEW |

#### 8. Cycle types (`cy`)
| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `o` | one-time |
| `m` | monthly |
| `q` | quarterly |
| `a` | annual |

#### 9. BIN/IIN metadata
- `bn` can appear at bank, group, or card level
- Subkeys: `px` (exact prefixes), `rg` (ranges), `ln` (valid lengths)
- BIN is a **hint**, not unique truth. Low-confidence BINs allowed (per option 2 strategy).
- May be **omitted entirely** for low-confidence cards.

#### 10. Upto structure (`up`)
- `null` or object:
  - `{"t":"sp","v":20000}` → spend cap
  - `{"t":"rw","v":1000}` → reward cap

#### 11. Modified structure (`md`)
Used when a perk is common to a group but differs for specific cards. Only store fields that differ.

#### 12. Confidence (`cf`)
- `h` = high (verified)
- `m` = medium (card exists; major perks correct; minor details unverified)
- `l` = low (card exists; minimal perk data; bank-level inheritance only)

